Batch validation keeps per-row provenance, never prints parameters and keeps
running after bad rows.

```console
$ keyscope validate --csv-in audit.csv --config fake-providers.yaml --dry-run --no-banner
? 1
❗ row 2 fakeok success: validation passed
row 3 fakefail failure: validation failed: status_code
row 4 unknown-provider error: unknown provider
row 5 error: missing provider name
row 6 fakeok error: no parameters provided
row 7 fakeok success: validation passed

Processed 6 row(s)

Success: 2
Failure: 1
  Error: 3

```

Repeated credentials stay traceable through their stable row numbers, and the
JSON reporter exposes the same sanitized per-row structure.

```console
$ keyscope validate --csv-in audit.csv --config fake-providers.yaml --dry-run --no-banner --reporter json
? 1
❗ [
  {
    "row": 2,
    "provider": "fakeok",
    "status": "success",
    "summary": "validation passed"
  },
  {
    "row": 3,
    "provider": "fakefail",
    "status": "failure",
    "summary": "validation failed: status_code"
  },
  {
    "row": 4,
    "provider": "unknown-provider",
    "status": "error",
    "summary": "unknown provider"
  },
  {
    "row": 5,
    "provider": "",
    "status": "error",
    "summary": "missing provider name"
  },
  {
    "row": 6,
    "provider": "fakeok",
    "status": "error",
    "summary": "no parameters provided"
  },
  {
    "row": 7,
    "provider": "fakeok",
    "status": "success",
    "summary": "validation passed"
  }
]

```

The quiet reporter suppresses output while preserving the non-zero exit code.

```console
$ keyscope validate --csv-in audit.csv --config fake-providers.yaml --dry-run --no-banner --reporter quiet
? 1

```

A fully healthy batch exits successfully.

```console
$ keyscope validate --csv-in all-ok.csv --config fake-providers.yaml --dry-run --no-banner --reporter quiet
? 0

```

Malformed CSV headers are rejected before any validation runs.

```console
$ keyscope validate --csv-in bad-header.csv --config fake-providers.yaml --no-banner
? 1
❗ csv file must start with a 'provider' header column

```
